.TH CF-ZONES 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-zones.1 \- Manage Cloudflare domain zones, settings, and analytics
.PP
Manage Cloudflare domain zones, inspect zone details, configure zone settings, and retrieve analytics dashboards.
.PP
.PP
.SH REQUIRED PERMISSIONS
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
Read
\fIMinimum Cloudflare API Token Scope:\fR \fBZone.Zone:Read\fR
.TP
Edit
\fIMinimum Cloudflare API Token Scope:\fR \fBZone.Zone:Edit\fR
.TP
Settings Edit
\fIMinimum Cloudflare API Token Scope:\fR \fBZone.Zone Settings:Edit\fR
.TP
Analytics
\fIMinimum Cloudflare API Token Scope:\fR \fBZone.Analytics:Read\fR
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH SUBCOMMANDS OVERVIEW
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf zones list\fR (#cf-zones-list) — List all zones in account
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf zones get\fR (#cf-zones-get) — Get detailed zone metadata
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf zones create\fR (#cf-zones-create) — Register a new zone
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf zones delete\fR (#cf-zones-delete) — Delete a zone
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf zones settings\fR (#cf-zones-settings) — Inspect and update zone settings
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf zones analytics\fR (#cf-zones-analytics) — View dashboard, colocation, and DNS traffic analytics
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf zones list\fR"
.PP
Lists all domain zones accessible by the active profile.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones list [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--account-id <id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR auto-detected | \fIDescription:\fR Filter zones by Account ID
.TP
\fB--name <domain>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Filter zones matching domain name
.TP
\fB--status <status>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Filter by status (\fBactive\fR, \fBpending\fR, \fBinitializing\fR, \fBmoved\fR, \fBdeleted\fR)
.TP
\fB--page <num>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDefault:\fR \fB1\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Page number for pagination
.TP
\fB--per-page <num>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDefault:\fR \fB20\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Number of results per page
.TP
\fB--all\fR
\fIType:\fR boolean | \fIDefault:\fR \fBfalse\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Fetch all zones across all pages automatically
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List all zones in table format
cf zones list

# Find active zones matching a domain prefix
cf zones list --name example.com --status active

# Fetch every zone across all pages
cf zones list --all
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf zones get\fR"
.PP
Displays comprehensive details for a specific zone.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones get --zone <zone-id-or-name>
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--zone <id-or-name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIRequired:\fR Yes | \fIDescription:\fR Zone ID or domain name (e.g. \fBexample.com\fR)
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones get --zone example.com
cf zones get --zone 023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf zones create\fR"
.PP
Creates a new domain zone within an account.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones create --name <domain> [--account-id <id>] [--type <type>] [--jump-start]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--name <domain>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Apex domain name (e.g., \fBexample.com\fR)
.TP
\fB--account-id <id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR auto-detected | \fIDescription:\fR Account ID where the zone will reside
.TP
\fB--type <type>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fBfull\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Zone setup type: \fBfull\fR (Cloudflare NS) or \fBpartial\fR (CNAME setup)
.TP
\fB--jump-start\fR
\fIType:\fR boolean | \fIDefault:\fR \fBfalse\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Automatically scan and import existing DNS records
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones create --name example.com --jump-start
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf zones delete\fR"
.PP
Deletes a zone from your Cloudflare account.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones delete --zone <zone-id-or-name> [--yes]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--zone <id-or-name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Zone ID or domain name to delete
.TP
\fB--yes\fR
\fIType:\fR boolean | \fIDescription:\fR Bypass interactive deletion confirmation prompt
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones delete --zone example.com --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf zones settings\fR"
.PP
Manage TLS, security, and caching settings for a zone.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List all settings and their current status
cf zones settings list --zone example.com

# Inspect a single setting (e.g., ssl, always_use_https, min_tls_version)
cf zones settings get --zone example.com --setting ssl

# Update a setting value
cf zones settings update --zone example.com --setting always_use_https --value on
cf zones settings update --zone example.com --setting min_tls_version --value "1.3"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf zones analytics\fR"
.PP
Retrieve traffic, performance, and threat metrics.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# General traffic and request dashboard
cf zones analytics dashboard --zone example.com --from 2024-01-01 --to 2024-01-31

# Edge colocation datacenter analytics
cf zones analytics colo --zone example.com

# DNS query traffic metrics
cf zones analytics dns --zone example.com
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
